  "method": "Batch of 513 witnesses in 22 problems (`MANIFEST.json` + `records/<record_id>.json` + `SUMMARY.tsv`), each at least 1e-4 (relative) below the current `records/SUMMARY.csv` entry (main at cbf76f2f, checked 2026-10-25). Every record passes `verify_general.py` (VALID) and `certify_general.py` (CERTIFIED) from that commit locally. 211 records improve by \u2265 1 %, 398 by \u2265 0.1 %.\n\nEach record starts from the current catalogue configuration for the same problem and n, or, where `derived_from` is set (278 records), from the first n pieces of the configuration for a larger n. Following the form's guidance for refinements, `found_by`, `credit` and `method` are kept exactly as in the seed record, and the refinement is named separately in `refined_by`, `refinement_credit` and `refinement`. The contact equations showed that s was not fixed by the contacts; I moved along the contact-preserving directions that decrease s and re-detected contacts. Rigidity analysis and code: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23630728\n\n**One new construction.** octintet n = 30, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35, 84, 98, 99, 100 are subsets of the alternating tetrahedral\u2013octahedral honeycomb, which tiles a tetrahedron of edge k with (k \u2212 1)k(k + 1)/6 unit octahedra (35 for k = 6, 84 for k = 8, 120 for k = 9); centres scaled by s/k for clearance. The current records for these n are above the honeycomb value k (for example 45/7 for n = 31\u201335). These records carry my own `found_by`.\n\nClearance: centres expanded by 3e-7 about the origin, container sized from the vertices for a 2e-7 wall gap, `s_full` rounded up at the 13th decimal. Each record also has `s_tight` (the touching value of the configuration); for 54 records whose s is fixed by the contacts there is `closed_form_conjecture`, with `closed_form_poly` and `closed_form_digits` (agreement with s computed to 120 digits). Closed forms for current records that this batch does not change are in a separate issue.\n\nPer problem:\